# Drop Sorter REST API v1 (httpyac / VS Code REST Client).
# Turn it on in Settings › General › API (or run `dropsorter serve`), then "Copy Token" and put it
# into the variable below. Never commit a real token.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:47800/v1
@token = {{$processEnv DROPSORTER_TOKEN}}

### Health (no token needed)
GET {{base}}/health

### Target folders, optionally filtered like the chooser
GET {{base}}/folders?q=fin%20inv
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Suggest a folder for names or paths
POST {{base}}/suggest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"names": ["Rechnung_Swisscom_2026-09.pdf", "Scans/"], "limit": 5}

### Preview a move (nothing is touched)
POST {{base}}/sort
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paths": ["/Users/me/Downloads/invoice-acme.pdf"], "auto": true, "dryRun": true}

### Copy into an explicit folder
POST {{base}}/sort
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paths": ["/Users/me/Desktop/contract.pdf"], "folder": "80 Backup", "mode": "copy"}

### What undo would revert
GET {{base}}/last
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Undo the most recent operation (optionally only if it is still operation "id")
POST {{base}}/undo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Configuration (read only)
GET {{base}}/config
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Drop apps
GET {{base}}/drop-apps
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
